// Named time zones: the TZif files RFC 9636 defines, the POSIX TZ strings a
// file's footer carries, and the two questions a wall clock raises in a zone —
// which instant it names, and what happens when it names none or two.
//
// A separate package because a calendar with a zone database is not the same
// product as one without: a caller that formats an HTTP date should not have to
// carry the database, and a caller that does need it wants the whole of it.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moondate",
}
